# Fingerprints of individual Gitleaks findings that are not credentials.
#
# A fingerprint is commit:path:rule:line, so an entry exempts exactly one
# reported line in exactly one historical commit and nothing else: the same
# text in any later commit has a different fingerprint and is scanned again.
# That makes this file narrower than a `.gitleaks.toml` allowlist, which is
# why it is the right place for a false positive that has no synthetic value
# to pin (the guardrail in scripts/test_secret_scan_guardrails.py requires
# every allowlist line to carry a quoted literal it can rotate).
